schema_version: '1.0'
schema_type: project_graph
project_id: daily-driver
project_name: Daily Driver — Pi (sab-mini) + dsh harness (sab-air) port
description: 'Cleanly port Pi extensions/skills (sab-mini) and the dsh harness plugin
  surface (sab-air — ~/.dsh profiles/patches/presets, deepseek-harness source) into
  one daily driver, run split between the two hosts: Pi stays the interactive coding
  harness here, dsh stays the agent harness on sab-air, with named cross-host seams.
  Freeze the two-host inventory, classify tiers, confirm the split, package each side,
  define policies, name capability twins, then dogfood both hosts.'
repo: local (sab-mini ~/.pi/agent + sab-air ~/.dsh / ~/.config/deepseek-harness)
blueprint:
  vision: 'One curated, documented daily-driver environment spanning two hosts. sab-mini
    runs Pi (interactive coding harness, extensions + skills); sab-air runs dsh (deepseek-harness
    agent loop with hot-reloadable tools/providers, gddp agent preset, profiles/patches).
    The split is intentional and written, not an accident: each side curates its own
    package, the seams between them are named (Hermes grok bridge :8645, shared skills,
    receipt/dispatch cross-points), and the result is proven by a two-host dogfood
    session.'
  architecture_notes: 'Settled during re-charting (2026-08-23, after direct sab-air
    recon): dsh is REAL — an agent harness on sab-air. ~/.dsh holds settings.yaml,
    profiles/ (acp, web), patches/ (claude-code-grok, subagent-grok, subagent-qwen),
    .agent-presets/ (gddp), sessions/, storages/. Source at ~/.config/deepseek-harness:
    dsh-agent loop (packages/README.md), tools/ providers/prompt sections register
    as reversible effects and hot-reload, structured output is a scoped runtime, ctx.subagents.registerProvider()
    is an open seam, memory is append-only JSONL with compaction and durable children,
    orchestration via goals/skills/workflows/agent-bus. Pi also exists on sab-air
    — both hosts have pi and aa. The port = curate/package each side, never merge
    runtimes. Node 04 (split decision) is human: Sab''s "run split between there and
    here" gets formalized — what runs where and the named seams. Enable-set changes
    are proposed diffs, never applied by an executor. aa-cli TUI graph is charted
    separately at aa-cli-tui-pass.'
  major_capabilities:
  - two-host checked-in catalog (Pi side + dsh side) with tiers
  - confirmed split architecture with named cross-host seams
  - one installable Pi daily-driver package (sab-mini)
  - curated dsh daily-driver config (sab-air, hot-reload verified)
  - Pi settings.json + dsh settings.yaml policy diffs (unapplied)
  - capability twins across Pi / dsh / Hermes
  - two-host dogfood proof
graph_version: '1.1'
